#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# struve_h

#% text
# `struve_h(nu, z)` gives the Struve function `H_nu(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `H_nu(z)` is the particular solution of the inhomogeneous Bessel equation of DLMF 11.2.1, the series of `(-1)^k*(z/2)^(2k + nu + 1)/(gamma(k + 3/2)*gamma(k + nu + 3/2))`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
struve_h(0, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.5686566270482879

#% cell
struve_h(1, 2.5)
#% output
#= 0.8631542066565353

#% cell
struve_h(0.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.7989752939540048

#% cell
n(struve_h(0, 1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.5686566270482879509864228863223533

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Large arguments, where `H_0(x) - Y_0(x)` tends to `2/(pi x)`:

#% cell
struve_h(0, 100.0) - bessel_y(0, 100.0) - 2/(pi*100.0)
#% output
#= -6.36048240007514e-7

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative of `H_0` is `2/pi - H_1`, checked by a difference quotient:

#% cell
(struve_h(0, 1.0 + 1.0e-6) - struve_h(0, 1.0 - 1.0e-6))/2.0e-6 - (2/pi - struve_h(1, 1.0))
#% output
#= -5.4026005891216755e-11


#% text
# Half-integer orders are elementary:

#% cell
struve_h(1/2, x)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)/(pi^(1/2)*x^(1/2)) - cos(x)*2^(1/2)/(pi^(1/2)*x^(1/2))

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(struve_h(nu, x), x)
#% output
#= (1/2)*(-struve_h(1 + nu, x) + (1/2)^nu*x^nu/(pi^(1/2)*gamma(3/2 + nu)) + struve_h(-1 + nu, x))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `struve_l`, `bessel_j`, `bessel_y`, `anger_j`
